 ],
 "literal": "If touched, it burns, other than that, like the pain of love, if parted, can it burn, the fire?",
 "translation": "Fire burns only when it is touched; but unlike that, can fire burn even when one departs from it, as the pain of love does?",
 "modern": "நெருப்பு தொட்டால் மட்டுமே சுடும்; ஆனால் காமநோய் போல, விலகிச் சென்றால் சுடக்கூடிய வலிமை நெருப்புக்கு உண்டா?",
 "explanation": "In this couplet, the heroine compares the pain of separation from her beloved to physical fire. She points out that fire only burns a person upon physical contact. However, the affliction of love (காமநோய்) behaves in the opposite manner, burning and causing intense suffering precisely when the lovers are parted (விடின்). By asking if fire can burn from a distance, she emphasizes that the torment of separation is far more powerful and painful than actual fire.",
